Marker file: this package is installed by install-lazy.sh, not by a bulk run.
install.sh skips any directory containing a .nopackage file, which is what keeps
this package and the nvim package from both writing ~/.config/nvim during
"./install.sh" with no arguments. Naming it still works: "./install.sh nvim-lazy"
links the files without the backup step that install-lazy.sh does first.
